<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n37961" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">praesĭdālis</span></b>  or <b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">praesĭdĭālis</span></b> , e,
			adj.
		praeses, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>of</i> or <i>belonging to the governor
				of a province</i>, <i>gubernatorial</i>
			(postclass.): 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">jus, Treb. Poll. XXX. Tyr. 24: jussio,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Cod. Just. 4, 24, 11</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">judicium,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">ib. 9, 1, 18</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">officium,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Amm. 28, 1, 5</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">apparitor,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">id. 17, 3, 6</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">vir,</span>”
				<i>who has been a governor</i>,
				 <i><span class="en">Symm. Ep. 4, 71</span></i>
			.</div>
